The Okami District Public Prosecutors Office arrested three leaders of the Akamatsu Group this morning. Akamatsu Seijiro, 45, chairman. Ibuki Yuma, 31, executive vice president and former entertainer. Izumida Shotaro, 48, chief financial advisor and former media commentator. Charges: corporate fraud, embezzlement of ¥18B from employee pension funds, falsification of financial records, money laundering. The investigation was triggered by a whistleblower — a mid-level accountant protected under the Public Officials Integrity Act. Search warrants executed at Akamatsu Group headquarters in Okami and subsidiaries in Toyozawa at 6:00 AM. The Okami Times notes: the Akamatsu Group is one of Okaiken's top 5 corporate groups. ¥4.2T in assets. 12,000 employees. The chairman, the executive VP, and the CFO advisor are in custody. ¥18B embezzled from employee pension funds over three years. Shell companies in Balisca. The IAA Commission is reviewing the case. The CIRA concentration limits may be relevant. The Okami Times asks: who else knew? How many other Akamatsu Groups are there? And why did it take a whistleblower — not the SESC's routine audit — to expose ¥18B in missing pension funds?

'''WMO RULING: "DEFINITION OF PARTNER" — Zong Trade Bridge Not a "Partner"; Okaiken May Restrict Data Sharing; Ruling Has Implications for Castellano Investigation; "The Data Dispute Is No Longer Just About Data"'''
The World Maritime Organization ruled today: Zong Trade Bridge Ltd. does not meet the "partner" standard for maritime cargo data sharing under the 2024 Shendan Ocean Maritime Safety Agreement. The ruling means Okaiken may restrict maritime data sharing with entities connected to Zong Trade Bridge. OMA Director Nishimura: "The WMO has ruled. Okaiken will act in accordance with the ruling." The Okami Times notes: the Zong Trade Bridge connection to the MV Castellano is now formally recognised by an international body. The data dispute is no longer just about data. The ruling has implications for the Castellano investigation — the Zong Trade Bridge connection is not just a commercial relationship. It is a structural link between a Zong commercial entity and a drug trafficking chain.

